                                        "entry_id": "2abcdb71-d1f0-3204-b99b-e78d9efa6d96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To groom (a horse); to dress or rub down a horse with a curry comb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41bbe9e1-1081-444a-afb4-aec27208d75c",
                                                "sense_id": "715c11e0-a318-3c72-a0ab-94b6630b2016",
                                                "text": "Your short horse is soon curried."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b278f5d-e584-47e4-ab2a-de7afd60441b",
                                                "sense_id": "715c11e0-a318-3c72-a0ab-94b6630b2016",
                                                "text": "One day I was out in the barn and he drifted in. I was currying the horse and he set down on the wheelbarrow and begun to ask questions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "254f8406-309d-30bf-99a6-8d677536cef1",
                                        "entry_id": "2abcdb71-d1f0-3204-b99b-e78d9efa6d96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dress (leather) after it is tanned by beating, rubbing, scraping and colouring."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40a7cc18-d222-3d7e-9885-8475fc4cfa67",
                                        "entry_id": "2abcdb71-d1f0-3204-b99b-e78d9efa6d96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To beat, thrash; to drub."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fbf2f2d-d227-4a42-b493-f35c163ce0a0",
                                                "sense_id": "40a7cc18-d222-3d7e-9885-8475fc4cfa67",
                                                "text": "I have seen him curry a fellow's carcase handsomely."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "617fb167-0f57-4236-a100-88999e968e1d",
                                                "sense_id": "40a7cc18-d222-3d7e-9885-8475fc4cfa67",
                                                "text": "[…]By setting brother against brother / To claw and curry one another."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c6d3cd6-b8b6-3cf6-af07-89e0ffd72d8b",
                                        "entry_id": "2abcdb71-d1f0-3204-b99b-e78d9efa6d96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To try to win or gain (favour) by flattering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "370285b9-50ee-44e6-a0a1-e63f277e75a2",
                                                "sense_id": "3c6d3cd6-b8b6-3cf6-af07-89e0ffd72d8b",
                                                "text": "A middle-aged woman waves and calls to her, as if she, like the hungry reporters, were currying the girl's favor: Florence Aadland (Sarandon, in a wily, multilayered performance), Beverly's mother, wears an expression of maternal concern, though her self-serving motives become increasingly clear."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "curry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da272a36-01b1-3a82-baae-20b5e7c8a4ca",
                                        "entry_id": "b6ef1208-71f1-3e61-af84-0c53c07ac950",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To perform currying upon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecf26af4-a15d-42b4-888c-96220f49ada8",
                                                "sense_id": "da272a36-01b1-3a82-baae-20b5e7c8a4ca",
                                                "text": "The easiest way to curry parameters is to create a function that takes a parameter block and returns a function that will call the original function with the presupplied parameters as defaults […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f918b754-6355-430e-9849-8db552f44c94",
                                                "sense_id": "da272a36-01b1-3a82-baae-20b5e7c8a4ca",
                                                "text": "Next, we curry the avg function to 3 arguments and put it into an option."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "curry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1506e30-b8c9-3ea5-a85c-474510a81887",
                                        "entry_id": "c3a06928-adfa-3245-999f-822204f63a5f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To scurry; to ride or run hastily"
                                        ],
